#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10044..10783
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/8
msgid ""
"...You really love UMAs, don't you, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你真的很喜欢未知生物啊，奇科？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10811..11953
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/9
msgid ""
"You know what I think? I think UMAs should be\n"
"dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道我怎么想？未知生物\n"
"就该危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 12037..12775
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/10
msgid ""
"Otherwise where's the fun in hunting them?\n"
msgstr ""
"不然猎捕它们还有什么乐趣？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/0
msgid ""
"Did you see a quetzal, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你看到凤尾绿咬鹃了吗，SNAKE？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/1
#: codec/2/915/0x3939d0/28
msgid ""
"Yep.\n"
msgstr ""
"看到了。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/2
msgid ""
"What do you think? Did it look like a snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得呢？它看起来像蛇吗？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/3
msgid ""
"Huh? No, it didn't look like a snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？不，它不像蛇。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/4
msgid ""
"Oh, really? ...Must be different from the\n"
"quetzalcoatl, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，是吗？……那肯定和\n"
"羽蛇神不一样。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/5
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl?\n"
msgstr ""
"羽蛇神？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/6
msgid ""
"A winged snake from Mayan and Aztec legend.\n"
msgstr ""
"玛雅和阿兹特克传说中长翅膀的蛇。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/7
msgid ""
"A winged snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"长翅膀的蛇……\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/8
msgid ""
"Weird, right? I bet it's a UMA.\n"
msgstr ""
"很怪吧？我赌它是未知生物。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/9
msgid ""
"Amanda and everybody says Quetzalcoatl is a\n"
"quetzal in the form of a god.\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达他们说羽蛇神是\n"
"凤尾绿咬鹃化成的神。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/10
msgid ""
"But there's no way anybody'd mistake a snake for\n"
"a bird,\n"
msgstr ""
"但谁也不可能把蛇错认成\n"
"鸟，\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/11
msgid ""
"I think the legend of Quetzalcoatl came first.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得羽蛇神的传说更早。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/12
msgid ""
"Somebody saw it and adopted it as their god,\n"
"before they saw the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人先看到它，奉为神，\n"
"之后才看到凤尾绿咬鹃。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/13
msgid ""
"After that, somebody saw a bird that looked like\n"
"the image of the god,\n"
msgstr ""
"后来有人看到一只鸟长得像\n"
"神的形象，\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/14
msgid ""
"and so they named it \"quetzal.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"就把它命名为“凤尾绿咬鹃”。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/15
msgid ""
"You mean it happened the other way around?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说反过来了？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/16
msgid ""
"If you ask me, the quetzalcoatl was probably a\n"
"pterosaur that survived.\n"
msgstr ""
"要我说，羽蛇神很可能就是幸存下来的\n"
"翼龙。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/17
msgid ""
"I mean, it's got wings, and it's a reptile, so it\n"
"probably looks kind of like a snake, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"它有翅膀，又是爬行动物，所以\n"
"大概有点像蛇，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/18
msgid ""
"Pterosaurs live on in Africa even today. They're\n"
"called the Kongamato and the Olitiau.\n"
msgstr ""
"翼龙至今仍生活在非洲。它们\n"
"被称为孔加马托和奥利提奥。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/19
msgid ""
"So it makes sense that there'd be pterosaurs on\n"
"the American continent, too,\n"
msgstr ""
"所以美洲大陆上也有翼龙，\n"
"这也说得通，\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/20
msgid ""
"and that they survived until the Mayan and Aztec\n"
"eras.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们一直活到玛雅和阿兹特克\n"
"时代。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/21
msgid ""
"Lucky for us they're not still around today.\n"
msgstr ""
"幸好它们现在不在了。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/22
msgid ""
"Who says they aren't? The dinosaurs supposedly\n"
"died out 65 million years ago,\n"
msgstr ""
"谁说不是呢？据说恐龙\n"
"在6500万年前就灭绝了，\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/23
msgid ""
"and the Aztec civilization only arose about 600\n"
"years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"而阿兹特克文明大约在600\n"
"年前才兴起。\n"

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/24
msgid ""
"If they managed to survive 65 million years, surely\n"
"they couldn't be wiped out in 600.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果它们能存活6500万年，那肯定\n"
"不可能在600年里就被消灭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1922
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/0
msgid ""
"A base disguised as a mine? We never made it\n"
"that far.\n"
msgstr ""
"伪装成矿场的基地？我们从来没到过\n"
"那么远的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 1964..3162
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/1
msgid ""
"I don't know what kind of place it is, but you'd\n"
"better be careful - just in case.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道那是什么地方，但你\n"
"最好小心点——以防万一。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3496
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/2
msgid ""
"I plan to.\n"
msgstr ""
"会的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3510..5196
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/3
msgid ""
"I've heard that the American army keeps dead alien\n"
"bodies and UFOs in secret bases.\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说美军把外星人尸体和UFO\n"
"藏在秘密基地里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5461..5726
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/4
msgid ""
"Aliens?\n"
msgstr ""
"外星人？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5726..6325
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/5
msgid ""
"There are billions of stars in space.\n"
msgstr ""
"太空里有几十亿颗恒星。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7523
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/6
msgid ""
"You've gotta think that at least a few have\n"
"civilizations more advanced than ours.\n"
msgstr ""
"你肯定得想，至少有几个\n"
"文明比我们更先进。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8526
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/7
msgid ""
"I'll bet they visit Earth in UFOs.\n"
msgstr ""
"我赌他们坐UFO来过地球。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 8596..9055
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/8
msgid ""
"In 1947,\n"
msgstr ""
"1947年\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 9083..10602
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/9
msgid ""
"the army actually announced they'd caught a flying,\n"
"disc-shaped object near Roswell, New Mexico.\n"
msgstr ""
"军方竟宣布在新墨西哥州罗斯威尔附近\n"
"抓到个飞行的碟形物体。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 10699..11828
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/10
msgid ""
"Maybe you don't know about it, but those army\n"
"guys, they all know!\n"
msgstr ""
"也许你不知道，但那些军方\n"
"的人全知道！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12176..12455
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/11
msgid ""
"You don't say...\n"
msgstr ""
"不会吧……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12455..13736
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/12
msgid ""
"Anyway, there's no telling what kind of mystery\n"
"weapons they might have stashed up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"总之，谁也说不准他们在那里藏了\n"
"什么样的神秘武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 13848..14182
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/13
msgid ""
"Watch your back.\n"
msgstr ""
"小心点。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/0
msgid ""
"Apparently, UFOs are connected to cattle\n"
"mutilations.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说，UFO与牛只\n"
"残杀事件有关。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/1
msgid ""
"Cattle mutations?\n"
msgstr ""
"牛变异了？\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/2
msgid ""
"Not mutations. Mutilations... It's a word I'd never\n"
"heard before.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是变异，是残杀……这词我以前\n"
"从没听过。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/3
msgid ""
"People have been reporting their livestock dying\n"
msgstr ""
"有人报告自家牲口死得\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/4
msgid ""
"in mysterious ways near the same places where\n"
"UFOs have been sighted.\n"
msgstr ""
"很蹊跷，地点都在目击UFO的\n"
"附近。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/5
msgid ""
"They say\n"
msgstr ""
"他们说\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/6
msgid ""
"the bodies are drained of blood and the eyeballs\n"
"and sexual organs are gouged out.\n"
msgstr ""
"尸体被抽干了血，眼球和\n"
"生殖器都被挖走了。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/7
msgid ""
"When you leave a corpse cut open in a field\n"
"somewhere, the ground soaks up the blood.\n"
msgstr ""
"把尸体剖开扔在野地里，\n"
"血会被土地吸干。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/8
msgid ""
"Yeah, but supposedly these cows weren't cut up\n"
"by any man-made means.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但据说这些牛不是\n"
"人为切割的。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/9
msgid ""
"Maybe maggots got to 'em?\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是蛆啃的？\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/10
msgid ""
"In some cases they detected radiation.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些案例还检测到了辐射。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/11
msgid ""
"Radiation...\n"
msgstr ""
"辐射……\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/12
msgid ""
"Even in our own town we had goats that died in\n"
"strange ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"就连我们镇上也有山羊\n"
"死得很怪。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/13
msgid ""
"Some said they saw a monster\n"
msgstr ""
"有人说见过怪物\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/14
msgid ""
"- a lizard on two legs, covered in spines from its\n"
"head all the way down its back.\n"
msgstr ""
"——两条腿的蜥蜴，从脑袋到\n"
"后背全长满尖刺。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/15
msgid ""
"I wonder if that's what the aliens look like,\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道外星人是不是就长这样，\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/16
msgid ""
"or if it was some pet they brought with them...\n"
msgstr ""
"还是他们带来的宠物……\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/17
msgid ""
"...Either way, it doesn't sound like a very advanced\n"
"civilization to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不管怎样，听起来都不像\n"
"什么高级文明。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/18
msgid ""
"If you see one, tell it I said \"hi!\"\n"
msgstr ""
"见到就替我向它问好！\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/19
msgid ""
"Sure... if it speaks human.\n"
msgstr ""
"行……前提是它说人话。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4f20/0
msgid ""
"UFOs kidnap people, too - you know, alien\n"
"abductions.\n"
msgstr ""
"UFO也会绑架人类，\n"
"就是所谓的外星人劫持。\n"

#: codec/1/212/0xd4f20/1
msgid ""
"You've heard of the Hill Abduction, right? That\n"
"couple back in the 60s.\n"
msgstr ""
"你听说过希尔夫妇劫持案吧？\n"
"就是60年代的那对夫妇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 459..1532
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/0
msgid ""
"You wanna know something? I once met an alien\n"
"cat.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟你说，我见过一只外星\n"
"猫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 1546..2229
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/1
msgid ""
"An alien... cat?\n"
msgstr ""
"外星猫？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 2243..3051
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/2
msgid ""
"Yep. It was dark out so I couldn't see too well,\n"
msgstr ""
"对。当时天很黑，看不太清，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3120..3956
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/3
msgid ""
"but it was a cat with a huge long tail.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那猫的尾巴又大又长。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3998..4500
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/4
msgid ""
"Its eyes shined in the dark, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"眼睛在黑暗里还发光。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 4513..4987
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/5
msgid ""
"Most cats' eyes do...\n"
msgstr ""
"猫的眼睛大多都这样……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 5001..6854
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/6
msgid ""
"At first I thought it was a regular cat. But then it\n"
"started talking to me - inside my head.\n"
msgstr ""
"一开始我以为只是只普通的猫。但它\n"
"开始跟我说话——在我脑子里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 6868..7230
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/7
msgid ""
"...Inside your head?\n"
msgstr ""
"……在你脑子里？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 7230..8345
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/8
msgid ""
"He said his name was Altargozo Elbakki Munyudar.\n"
msgstr ""
"它说自己叫Altargozo Elbakki Munyudar。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 8400..9682
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/9
msgid ""
"He'd come to Earth from the Andromeda Galaxy to\n"
"check out Earth's nuclear weapons...\n"
msgstr ""
"它从仙女座星系来到地球，\n"
"调查地球的核武器……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 9724..10992
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/10
msgid ""
"The Andromeda Galaxy... Mankind's barely made it\n"
"to the moon.\n"
msgstr ""
"仙女座星系……人类才勉强\n"
"登上月球。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11089..11702
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/11
msgid ""
"We couldn't possibly launch nukes that far.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不可能把核弹发射那么远。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11716..13054
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/12
msgid ""
"Elbakki said he was watching over us - to make\n"
"sure we don't destroy ourselves with nukes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Elbakki说它在守护我们——确保\n"
"我们不会用核弹毁灭自己。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 13123..14113
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/13
msgid ""
"Until the day we humans are ready to join the\n"
"Space Federation...\n"
msgstr ""
"直到人类准备好加入\n"
"星际联邦的那一天……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 14489..15659
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/14
msgid ""
"...It's a shame. This is supposed to be the era of\n"
"Détente,\n"
msgstr ""
"……真可悲。这明明该是\n"
"缓和的年代，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 15729..16899
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/15
msgid ""
"and still we've got people pulling stunts like\n"
"bringing nukes into peaceful countries.\n"
msgstr ""
"却还有人把核武器带进\n"
"和平国家，搞这种把戏。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 16941..18111
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/16
msgid ""
"If something ever went wrong and set off a chain\n"
"reaction of retaliation...\n"
msgstr ""
"万一出了差错，引发报复的\n"
"连锁反应……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 18111..19379
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/17
msgid ""
"I know. This planet could destroy itself at anytime.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。这颗星球随时可能自我毁灭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/0
msgid ""
"Snake, is it true you took a picture of el colibri?\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，你真的拍到蜂鸟了吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1964
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/1
msgid ""
"Yep. Got it right here.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。就在这儿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1978..4026
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/2
msgid ""
"Whoa! It's like an actual UFO! I knew it - los\n"
"yanquis are working with the aliens!\n"
msgstr ""
"哇！简直像真的UFO！我就知道——\n"
"美国佬在跟外星人合作！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4221..4973
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/3
msgid ""
"I know it kind of looks that way, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道看起来有点像，但……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5684
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/4
msgid ""
"Hey Snake, can you make me a copy of that?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿SNAKE，能给我复制一份吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 5698..6506
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/5
msgid ""
"I don't see why not. What for?\n"
msgstr ""
"行啊。干嘛？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 6520..7871
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/6
msgid ""
"People pay good money for this stuff. We can use\n"
"it to raise money for MSF.\n"
msgstr ""
"这东西能卖不少钱。我们可以\n"
"用它给MSF筹款。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 7927..9181
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/7
msgid ""
"Ha, sure, kid. You go out and get us a good price\n"
"for it.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈，行啊小子。你去给我们\n"
"卖个好价钱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 9195..10518
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/8
msgid ""
"You don't believe me, do you? I'll get the money.\n"
"You'll see!\n"
msgstr ""
"你不信我，是吧？我会拿到钱。\n"
"你等着瞧！\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, legend has it a place called Isla del\n"
"Monstruo is near Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，传说哥斯达黎加附近\n"
"有个叫怪物岛的地方。\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/1
msgid ""
"Isla del Monstruo?\n"
msgstr ""
"怪物岛？\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/2
msgid ""
"It was discovered in the 18th century by\n"
"Caribbean pirates sailing over to the Pacific.\n"
msgstr ""
"18世纪时，前往太平洋的\n"
"加勒比海盗发现了它。\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/3
msgid ""
"And the island in \"Treasure Island\" - it's based on\n"
"one near Costa Rica, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"《金银岛》里的那座岛，\n"
"原型也在哥斯达黎加附近。\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/4
msgid ""
"\"Treasure Island?\" I remember reading that.\n"
msgstr ""
"《金银岛》？我记得读过。\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/5
msgid ""
"You've read it too? That makes things easier.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也读过？那就好说了。\n"

#: codec/1/213/0xd5dd0/6
msgid ""
"In Nicaragua we too have a story about a group of\n"
"pirates that encountered\n"
msgstr ""
"我们尼加拉瓜也有个传说，\n"
"讲一群海盗遭遇了……\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/0
msgid ""
"Chico. I, uh... I met that talking cat.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科。我，呃……我见到那只说话的猫了。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/1
msgid ""
"The legendary Trenya? Really?!\n"
msgstr ""
"传说Trenya？真的？！\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/2
msgid ""
"Trenya? Yeah, that's what it called itself. Is it\n"
"famous?\n"
msgstr ""
"Trenya？对，它这么自称。它\n"
"很有名吗？\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/3
msgid ""
"In certain circles, yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"在某些圈子里，是的。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/4
msgid ""
"I'm still having trouble believing it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我还是难以相信。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/5
msgid ""
"I never thought I'd be talking to an animal one day.\n"
"What a world.\n"
msgstr ""
"没想到有一天我会跟动物说话。\n"
"这世道啊。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/6
msgid ""
"Amazing you could understand its language.\n"
msgstr ""
"你居然能听懂它的话，厉害。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/7
msgid ""
"Picking up the local lingo is one of the basics of\n"
"intelligence work.\n"
msgstr ""
"学会当地的语言是\n"
"情报工作的基本功之一。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/8
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the Boss, Boss! Hey, say\n"
"something in Trenya's language, will you?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你是老板，老板！嘿，用特雷尼亚的话\n"
"说点什么吧？\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/9
msgid ""
"Meow? Meow... Meow meow meow...\n"
msgstr ""
"喵？喵……喵喵喵……\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/10
msgid ""
"Wow! I have no idea what you're saying!\n"
msgstr ""
"哇！我完全听不懂！\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/11
msgid ""
"...Of course you wouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你当然不懂。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/12
msgid ""
"So what did Trenya say?\n"
msgstr ""
"Trenya说了啥？\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/13
msgid ""
"It said it would take me to that island you talked\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""
"它说会带我去你提到的\n"
"那座岛。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/14
msgid ""
"Really?! Take me too, Boss! Please, please!\n"
msgstr ""
"真的？！BOSS带我去！求你了！\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/15
msgid ""
"I know you must be excited, but we don't know\n"
"what's out there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道你很兴奋，但我们不知道\n"
"那里有什么。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/16
msgid ""
"It could be dangerous. I'll scout it out first.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能有危险。我先去侦察。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/17
msgid ""
"No fair!\n"
msgstr ""
"不公平！\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/18
msgid ""
"Come on, Chico. This isn't as cut and dry as you\n"
"think.\n"
msgstr ""
"别这样，奇科。这事可不像你\n"
"想的那么简单。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/19
msgid ""
"You can come next time, depending on what I find.\n"
msgstr ""
"看情况，下次带你去。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/20
msgid ""
"I'll take some photos if I get the chance. Sorry,\n"
"kid, but that's life.\n"
msgstr ""
"有机会就拍些照片。抱歉，\n"
"孩子，生活就是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/0
msgid ""
"Apparently there are other cats that talk besides\n"
"Trenya on Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说怪物岛上，除了特雷尼亚，\n"
"还有别的猫会说话。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/1
msgid ""
"There's more of them?\n"
msgstr ""
"还有更多？\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/2
msgid ""
"Yep. They're called the Felynes, but supposedly\n"
"they don't ever come to Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。它们叫随从猫，但据说\n"
"它们从来不会来哥斯达黎加。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/3
msgid ""
"You should try talking to them if you spot them.\n"
"Who knows what kinda stuff they have to say.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你看到它们，应该试着和它们说话。\n"
"谁知道它们会说些什么呢。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/4
msgid ""
"Yeah. Just when you think things can't get any\n"
"crazier...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。就在你以为事情不能再\n"
"更疯狂的时候……\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/5
msgid ""
"Also, the Felynes are nice to humans, so you be\n"
"sure and be nice back.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，随从猫对人类很友善，所以你\n"
"也一定要对它们友善。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/6
msgid ""
"Don't you go attacking them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"别去攻击它们。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/7
msgid ""
"I would never hurt a defenseless little kitty.\n"
msgstr ""
"我绝不会伤害毫无防备的小猫。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/0
msgid ""
"I used to have this book full of pirate lore.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以前有本讲海盗传说的书。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/1
msgid ""
"It had this story about Rathalos, King of the Skies.\n"
msgstr ""
"书里写了天空之王火龙的传说。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/2
msgid ""
"Most accounts describe it as a dragon with wings,\n"
"or a wyvern.\n"
msgstr ""
"多数记载说它是有翼的龙，\n"
"或者说是双足飞龙。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/3
msgid ""
"A wyvern... A two-legged dragon. Vlad the Impaler's\n"
"coat of arms had one on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"双足飞龙……两条腿的龙。\n"
"穿刺公弗拉德的纹章上就有。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/4
msgid ""
"Yeah, and he was the model for Count Dracula.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，他还是德古拉伯爵的原型。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/5
msgid ""
"There are reports of ships being attacked out in\n"
"the middle of the ocean,\n"
msgstr ""
"有报告称船只在\n"
"大洋中央遭到袭击，\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/6
msgid ""
"so Rathalos must be able to fly great distances.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以火龙一定能长距离飞行。\n"

#: codec/1/214/0xd6dc0/7
msgid ""
"And what's more, Rathalos is said to breathe fire!\n"
msgstr ""
"而且据说火龙还会喷火！\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/0
msgid ""
"Tigrex is a wyvern just like Rathalos.\n"
msgstr ""
"轰龙和火龙一样是飞龙。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/1
msgid ""
"But it's good at moving around on land, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"但它在陆地上也很灵活。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/2
msgid ""
"It can blast you with rocks from a distance, or\n"
"rush at you with incredible speed.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能在远处用岩石轰击你，或者\n"
"以惊人的速度冲向你。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/3
msgid ""
"People have seen it on land?\n"
msgstr ""
"有人在陆地见过它？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/4
msgid ""
"Sí.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/5
msgid ""
"It's said that these two lady pirates, Anne and\n"
"Mary, visited Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说这两位女海盗，安妮和\n"
"玛丽，曾到访过怪物岛。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/6
msgid ""
"It was there that they did battle with Tigrex.\n"
msgstr ""
"她们在那里与轰龙交战。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/7
msgid ""
"Anne was quite a marksman, wasn't she?\n"
msgstr ""
"安妮枪法很准吧？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/8
msgid ""
"Must've been a heck of a battle. I wish I'd been\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"那一定是场恶战。真希望我当时\n"
"在场。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/9
msgid ""
"You know, I'm not so bad with guns myself...\n"
msgstr ""
"说起来，我枪法也不差……\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/10
msgid ""
"I've already seen how good you are.\n"
msgstr ""
"你的本事我见识过了。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/0
msgid ""
"Anne and Mary also saw little dinosaurs running\n"
"around the island.\n"
msgstr ""
"安妮和玛丽还看到小恐龙在\n"
"岛上四处奔跑。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/1
msgid ""
"Velocipreys?\n"
msgstr ""
"迅猛龙？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/2
msgid ""
"Yup. As you'd expect they're very nimble - but no\n"
"match for a firearm.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。如你所料，它们很敏捷，但\n"
"敌不过火器。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/3
msgid ""
"You wouldn't want to get surrounded by them,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过，你可不想被它们\n"
"包围。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/4
msgid ""
"I'll bet. Nobody wants to be outnumbered in battle.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是。没人想在战斗中被围。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/5
msgid ""
"Right. Your best move would be to make sure they\n"
"cannot encircle you.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。你最好的做法是确保它们\n"
"无法包围你。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/6
msgid ""
"Well, stealth is the basis of all solo sneaking\n"
"missions...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，潜行是所有单人潜入\n"
"任务的基础……\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/7
msgid ""
"While it makes battle tougher,\n"
msgstr ""
"虽然战斗会更艰难，\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/8
msgid ""
"working alone has its advantages when it comes to\n"
"infiltration.\n"
msgstr ""
"在渗透方面，独自\n"
"行动有它的优势。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/9
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the boss, Boss! You don't\n"
"need any advice from me.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你是老大，老大！你\n"
"不用听我的建议。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/10
msgid ""
"Not bad for an old-timer, eh Chico?\n"
msgstr ""
"老将宝刀未老吧，奇科？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/11
msgid ""
"Nope. Still, be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，但要小心。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard the legend about the dinosaur that\n"
"came back to life as a zombie\n"
msgstr ""
"你听说过那个关于恐龙\n"
"作为僵尸复活的传说吗\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/1
msgid ""
"and attacked people?\n"
msgstr ""
"袭击人类？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/2
msgid ""
"Zombie?! You mean the living dead?\n"
msgstr ""
"僵尸？！你是说活死人？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/3
msgid ""
"Yeah. Dinosaurs may be extinct,\n"
msgstr ""
"对。恐龙虽然灭绝了，\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/4
msgid ""
"but technically it would be possible for one to\n"
"come back to life as a zombie.\n"
msgstr ""
"但理论上有可能\n"
"以僵尸形态复活。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/5
msgid ""
"Not so fast. Dinosaurs were real, zombies... not so\n"
"much.\n"
msgstr ""
"别急。恐龙是真的，僵尸……\n"
"可不一定。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/6
msgid ""
"What are you talking about, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""
"BOSS，你在说什么！\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/7
msgid ""
"Zombies have been used as slaves on Haitian\n"
"plantations for years.\n"
msgstr ""
"多年来僵尸一直被当作奴隶\n"
"用在海地种植园里。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/8
msgid ""
"In Haiti they've handed down a secret zombie\n"
"powder for generations.\n"
msgstr ""
"在海地，一种秘密的僵尸粉\n"
"代代相传。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/10
msgid ""
"People from long ago must have used that same\n"
"stuff on dinosaur remains.\n"
msgstr ""
"古人肯定把同样的东西\n"
"用在了恐龙遗骸上。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/11
msgid ""
"But dinosaurs had been extinct for millions of\n"
"years before the first humans-\n"
msgstr ""
"可恐龙早在人类出现前\n"
"几百万年就灭绝了——\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/12
msgid ""
"That hypothesis has to be wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"那个假设肯定不对。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/13
msgid ""
"...In any case, this zombie was incredibly powerful.\n"
msgstr ""
"……总之，这只僵尸强得离谱。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/14
msgid ""
"Its name was Gear REX. They say nothing could kill\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"它的名字叫“齿轮暴龙”。据说没有什么能杀死\n"
"它。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/15
msgid ""
"Some say its bodily fluids would burn right through\n"
"your flesh.\n"
msgstr ""
"有人说它的体液能直接烧穿\n"
"你的皮肉。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/16
msgid ""
"Then the spines that fell off its back would impale\n"
"you,\n"
msgstr ""
"然后从它背上脱落的尖刺会刺穿\n"
"你，\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/17
msgid ""
"the pain made even worse by the deafening roar\n"
"rattling every bone in your body.\n"
msgstr ""
"震耳欲聋的咆哮震得你全身骨头\n"
"咯咯响，痛上加痛。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/18
msgid ""
"...You sure it wasn't just some really strong\n"
"monster?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你确定它不是\n"
"某种特别强的怪物？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/19
msgid ""
"Who knows what kind of dinosaurs were out there.\n"
msgstr ""
"谁知道世上有什么恐龙。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/20
msgid ""
"We could be talking about something strong\n"
"enough to resist small arms fire.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们说的可能是种\n"
"能扛住轻武器射击的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/21
msgid ""
"Are you afraid of zombies, Boss?\n"
msgstr ""
"BOSS，你怕僵尸吗？\n"

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/22
msgid ""
"...No. I just find the whole thing hard to believe.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不。我只是觉得难以置信。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/0
msgid ""
"A fantasma is an espiritu that wanders this plane\n"
"instead of going to el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""
"fantasma是一种espiritu，\n"
"不去el Cielo，而在人间游荡。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/1
msgid ""
"There are different interpretations, of course, but\n"
"that's what I think.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然有不同解释，\n"
"但我是这么理解的。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/2
msgid ""
"See, the fantasma has a reason for remaining in\n"
"this world.\n"
msgstr ""
"你看，fantasma留在世上\n"
"是有原因的。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/3
msgid ""
"And if that were, say, a deep hatred for someone,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果那原因是对某人的深仇大恨，\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/4
msgid ""
"they just might be capable of inflicting harm on\n"
"that person.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们或许真的能够伤害到\n"
"那个人。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/5
msgid ""
"You probably realize this, but your weapons or\n"
"CQC won't work on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""
"你应该也明白，武器和\n"
"CQC对幻影没用。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/6
msgid ""
"And since they're not physical beings, they can\n"
"pass right through solid objects.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们不是实体，能直接\n"
"穿过固体。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/7
msgid ""
"But, if you can eliminate their reason for remaining\n"
"here,\n"
msgstr ""
"但只要你能消灭它们\n"
"留在这里的理由，\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/8
msgid ""
"you should be able to help them reach el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""
"就能帮它们抵达天堂。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/9
msgid ""
"People say words can work wonders on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说言语对幻影有奇效。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/10
msgid ""
"You could try talking to them through CO-OPS\n"
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以试试用合作任务\n"
"通讯跟它们说话。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1504
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/0
msgid ""
"You can't always see fantasma with your naked eye.\n"
msgstr ""
"幻影不一定肉眼可见。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2967
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/1
msgid ""
"If some unseen presence is making a noise, you\n"
"can be sure one is around.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果有无形之物发出声响，\n"
"那附近肯定有一只。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2967..3956
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/2
msgid ""
"When that happens, try taking photos in the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"这时试着在周围拍照。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4583
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/3
msgid ""
"You should be able to see what's causing it.\n"
msgstr ""
"应该能拍到元凶。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5126
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/4
msgid ""
"Why do they show up on photos?\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么照片能拍到？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5168..5739
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/5
msgid ""
"I'm not the one to ask about that, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"这我可答不上来，不过……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5753..7537
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/6
msgid ""
"Maybe fantasma are somehow able to deceive our\n"
"minds - on a subconscious level.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许幻影能在潜意识层面\n"
"欺骗我们的心智。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 7551..9153
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/7
msgid ""
"They're right there in front of us, but they whisper,\n"
"\"Hey, we're not really here!\"\n"
msgstr ""
"它们就在眼前，却低语：\n"
"“嘿，我们不在那儿！”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10616
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/8
msgid ""
"But a camera is a machine, so they can't do\n"
"anything to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但相机是机器，它们\n"
"拿它没办法。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11466
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's it! That's gotta be it!\n"
msgstr ""
"对，就是这样！肯定是！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/0
msgid ""
"That's a rangefinder camera you have, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你拿的是测距相机吧，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2020
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/1
msgid ""
"Mi viejo used to talk about rangefinder cameras,\n"
msgstr ""
"我老爸以前常提测距相机，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3274
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/2
msgid ""
"and how they can focus just as well as any other\n"
"camera, despite their size.\n"
msgstr ""
"说它们虽小，对焦却\n"
"不输任何相机。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 3315..4193
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/3
msgid ""
"He also said they don't have much picture blur,\n"
"either.\n"
msgstr ""
"他还说这种相机\n"
"拍出来也不怎么糊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4207..4834
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/4
msgid ""
"To bring an object into focus,\n"
msgstr ""
"要对焦物体时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5893
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/5
msgid ""
"make sure the two images overlap before taking\n"
"the picture.\n"
msgstr ""
"拍照前先让两个影像\n"
"重叠。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6631
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/6
msgid ""
"But you could probably do that in your sleep,\n"
"couldn't you?\n"
msgstr ""
"但你大概闭着眼睛都能做到，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 6631..7871
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/7
msgid ""
"All you need to worry about is making sure your\n"
"subject is in the frame.\n"
msgstr ""
"你只需确保\n"
"被摄物在取景框内。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 7899..9181
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/8
msgid ""
"Remember, Snake, photography is all about timing.\n"
msgstr ""
"记住，SNAKE，摄影全靠时机。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/0
msgid ""
"Amanda is so bossy. It's always \"Follow me\" or\n"
"\"Stay here.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"阿曼达太爱发号施令了，\n"
"不是「跟我来」就是「待在这儿」。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/1
msgid ""
"The other day she told me, \"Chew your gallo pinto\n"
"before you swallow.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"前两天她还跟我说：\n"
"「把豆饭嚼碎了再咽。」\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/2
msgid ""
"Can you believe it?\n"
msgstr ""
"你能信吗？\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/3
msgid ""
"Knowing your sister? Yeah, I can.\n"
msgstr ""
"你姐姐的性子？我信。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/4
msgid ""
"The enemy could strike at any time.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人随时可能来袭。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/5
msgid ""
"I can't sit around taking my sweet time eating!\n"
msgstr ""
"我哪能慢悠悠地坐着吃饭！\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/6
msgid ""
"I'm a Sandinista just like the others.\n"
msgstr ""
"我跟其他人一样是桑地诺主义者。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/7
msgid ""
"I don't need some woman telling me what to do!\n"
msgstr ""
"用不着一个女人来指使我！\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/8
msgid ""
"...Some woman? She's your sister,\n"
msgstr ""
"……一个女人？她是你姐姐，\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/9
msgid ""
"and she's doing the best she can to fill your\n"
"father's shoes.\n"
msgstr ""
"她已经在尽力\n"
"接替你父亲的位置了。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/10
msgid ""
"I know, I know, but... lately, she hasn't been doing\n"
"so good.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道，我知道，可是……\n"
"最近她状态不太好。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/11
msgid ""
"I... Should be strong for her.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……该为她坚强起来。\n"

#: codec/1/216/0xd8d60/12
msgid ""
"Now you're talking.\n"
msgstr ""
"这才像话。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 459..891
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/0
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""
"你父亲的事，我很遗憾。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 905..2229
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/1
msgid ""
"Don't be. He was... He is a guerrilla warrior.\n"
msgstr ""
"不必。他曾是……游击战士。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3134
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/2
msgid ""
"We pledge our lives to our country and its people...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们为祖国和人民献出生命……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3705
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/3
msgid ""
"I'm ready to die, too, if I have to.\n"
msgstr ""
"必要时，我也准备赴死。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3733..3984
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/4
msgid ""
"You sure?\n"
msgstr ""
"你确定？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 4054..5600
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/5
msgid ""
"You'd better believe it! Like mi viejo used to say,\n"
"\"Patria o Muerte.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"当然！就像我老爹常说的，\n"
"“祖国或死亡。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6325
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/6
msgid ""
"Che said it first.\n"
msgstr ""
"切先说的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 6339..6924
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/7
msgid ""
"My dad used to tell us all kinds of stories.\n"
msgstr ""
"我爸常给我们讲各种故事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7857
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/8
msgid ""
"About General Sandino and his fight against la\n"
"Guardia...\n"
msgstr ""
"关于桑地诺将军和他对抗\n"
"国民警卫队……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8470
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/9
msgid ""
"And about my mom before she left us.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有我妈离开前的事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8512..8860
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/10
msgid ""
"You didn't want to go with her?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不想跟她走？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8874..10072
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/11
msgid ""
"It's not like that. La revolución comes first, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是那样。革命优先，仅此而已。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10142..10657
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/12
msgid ""
"You must wish you could see her, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过你一定想见她。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10671..12496
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/13
msgid ""
"I dunno. But I know I'll see her again when this is\n"
"all over. Somehow I just know it.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道。但我知道等一切结束后\n"
"会再见到她。我就是知道。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 12566..13890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/14
msgid ""
"When I do, me and mamá and papá are all going to\n"
"live together again.\n"
msgstr ""
"到那时，我和妈妈、爸爸\n"
"会重新住在一起。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 14210..14475
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/15
msgid ""
"At least...\n"
msgstr ""
"至少…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 15241..15631
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/16
msgid ""
"At least, that's what I thought.\n"
msgstr ""
"至少，我是这么想的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 17512..18529
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/17
msgid ""
"Hang in there, Chico. Your sister needs you.\n"
msgstr ""
"撑住，奇科。你姐姐需要你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 459..1880
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever heard, \"Shoot, coward, you are only\n"
"going to kill a man\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"你听过“开枪吧，懦夫，你不过\n"
"杀一个人”吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2256..2716
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/1
msgid ""
"Che's last words.\n"
msgstr ""
"切的遗言。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2730..3260
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/2
msgid ""
"He'd been captured in Bolivia,\n"
msgstr ""
"他在玻利维亚被捕，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 3315..4207
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/3
msgid ""
"and said it to the soldiers just as they were about\n"
"to execute him.\n"
msgstr ""
"并在士兵们即将处决他时\n"
"对他们说了这句话。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 4207..5182
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/4
msgid ""
"El Che... He was something, wasn't he?\n"
msgstr ""
"切……他真了不起，对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 5252..6227
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/5
msgid ""
"Coming up with a line like that knowing he was\n"
"about to die.\n"
msgstr ""
"明知自己即将死去，\n"
"还能想出这样一句话。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6241..6743
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/6
msgid ""
"After the Cuban Revolution,\n"
msgstr ""
"古巴革命之后，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6743..8094
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/7
msgid ""
"Che gave up his position in the new government to\n"
"aide in revolutions in other countries.\n"
msgstr ""
"切放弃了新政府中的职位，去\n"
"援助他国的革命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 8317..9473
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/8
msgid ""
"He knew he could die at any time, and he was\n"
"ready for it.\n"
msgstr ""
"他知道随时可能死，也早已\n"
"准备好了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 9487..10365
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/9
msgid ""
"Me, I couldn't take even a little torture...\n"
msgstr ""
"而我，连一点拷打都受不了……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 10407..11661
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/10
msgid ""
"But you've been reborn, as an hombre nuevo.\n"
"Right, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""
"但你已重生，成为了新人。\n"
"对吧，奇科？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 11674..11925
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/11
msgid ""
"Right...\n"
msgstr ""
"对…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/0
msgid ""
"Don't you ever get lonely living away from your\n"
"mom?\n"
msgstr ""
"离开妈妈生活，你从不觉得\n"
"孤单吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2173
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/1
msgid ""
"Not really. My compas are my family now.\n"
msgstr ""
"还好。同伴就是家人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2270..2786
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/2
msgid ""
"A lot of them are from the same village as me.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们很多人和我来自同一个村子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3538
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/3
msgid ""
"So you had plenty of people to take care of you.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以有很多人照顾你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/4
msgid ""
"Take care of me?! I'm a warrior, like any other\n"
"Sandinista!\n"
msgstr ""
"照顾我？！我是战士，和任何\n"
"桑地诺派一样！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5809
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/5
msgid ""
"We look out for each other. That is how it works.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们互相照应。就是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6645
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/6
msgid ""
"Sorry. Guess I misspoke.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。我说错话了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 6659..8150
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/7
msgid ""
"Now we're scattered because of that colibri... I\n"
"wonder where everybody went.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在我们因那只蜂鸟而四散……\n"
"不知道大家都去了哪里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9724
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/8
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake. If you see any Frente prisoners, please\n"
"you gotta get them out, OK?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，SNAKE。看到Frente俘虏，请\n"
"一定救他们出来，确定？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10964
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/9
msgid ""
"Those guys are solid - every one. You could use\n"
"them in MSF.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些家伙个个靠得住。你可以在\n"
"MSF用他们。\n"

#: codec/1/217/0xd9f30/0
msgid ""
"Hey Snake, are there any jobs for me here at\n"
"Mother Base? I can do anything!\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake，母基地有我能做的活吗？\n"
"我什么都能干！\n"

#: codec/1/217/0xd9f30/1
msgid ""
"You don't have to work, you know.\n"
msgstr ""
"你不用工作也没关系。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/0
msgid ""
"What's with all this sighing? You're not your usual\n"
"self.\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么一直叹气？你不太像平时的\n"
"自己。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/1
msgid ""
"Oh. Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。SNAKE。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/2
msgid ""
"Something on your mind?\n"
msgstr ""
"有心事？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/3
msgid ""
"Huh? No, not... really. Not really... I guess...\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯？没，没……真的。真的没有……大概吧……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/4
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，SNAKE……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/5
msgid ""
"Uh huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/6
msgid ""
"Girls are funny, y'know?\n"
msgstr ""
"女孩真难懂，你知道吗？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/7
msgid ""
"You can never tell what they're thinking, they're\n"
"always doing their own thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"你永远猜不透她们在想什么，总是\n"
"我行我素。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/8
msgid ""
"Maybe they really are different from us men...\n"
msgstr ""
"也许她们真和我们男人不一样……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/9
msgid ""
"Wh-what's this about now?\n"
msgstr ""
"什、怎么突然说这个？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/10
msgid ""
"Chico... do you have a crush on somebody?\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科……你有喜欢的人吗？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/11
msgid ""
"No! It's not that! I just...\n"
msgstr ""
"不！不是那样！我只是……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/12
msgid ""
"What? Go ahead, you can talk to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？说吧，跟我讲。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/13
msgid ""
"...Whenever I talk to Paz,\n"
msgstr ""
"……每次跟帕兹说话，\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/14
msgid ""
"my heart starts pounding and everything I say\n"
"comes out wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的心跳加速，说的话\n"
"全乱套了。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/15
msgid ""
"Paz? I guess she is... pretty close to your age.\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹？她跟你年纪倒是挺接近的。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/16
msgid ""
"That ever happen to you, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，你也遇过吗？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/17
msgid ""
"Well, sure. It happens to everybody.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。谁都会这样。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/18
msgid ""
"Well, how do I talk to her?\n"
msgstr ""
"那我该怎么跟她说话？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/19
msgid ""
"...That is a tough one.\n"
msgstr ""
"……这问题真难。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/20
msgid ""
"Uh... Why don't you try... talking to her like you talk\n"
"to everybody else?\n"
msgstr ""
"呃……你何不……像跟别人说话那样\n"
"跟她说话？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/21
msgid ""
"No... It doesn't work. I freeze up every time I'm\n"
"around her.\n"
msgstr ""
"不……没用。每次在她身边\n"
"我都会僵住。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/22
msgid ""
"Our eyes meet, and my face starts burning for\n"
"some reason...\n"
msgstr ""
"目光相遇，不知为何我的脸\n"
"开始发烫……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/23
msgid ""
"It's like living on the battlefield - you'll just have to\n"
"get used to it... her.\n"
msgstr ""
"就像生活在战场上——你只能\n"
"习惯它……习惯她。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/24
msgid ""
"You're nervous at first, but the more you're out\n"
"there, the more natural it feels.\n"
msgstr ""
"一开始你会紧张，但你出去的次数越多，\n"
"感觉就越自然。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/25
msgid ""
"Get your courage up and go talk to her more often.\n"
msgstr ""
"鼓起勇气，多去找她说话。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/27
msgid ""
"Man, girls are more full of mysteries than UMAs...\n"
msgstr ""
"唉，女人比未知生物还神秘……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/28
msgid ""
"You got that right.\n"
msgstr ""
"说得没错。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/0
msgid ""
"Chico, I heard you saw Paz trying to sabotage\n"
"ZEKE before she activated it.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科，我听说你看到帕兹在启动\n"
"ZEKE之前试图破坏它。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/1
msgid ""
"I should have stopped her...\n"
msgstr ""
"我本该拦住她的……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/2
msgid ""
"If only I hadn't run away...\n"
msgstr ""
"要是我没逃……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/3
msgid ""
"I could have captured her before she got inside...\n"
msgstr ""
"我本可以在她进去之前抓住她……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/4
msgid ""
"If I'd done that, she'd still be here...\n"
msgstr ""
"要是那样，她还会在这里……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/5
msgid ""
"She was carrying a gun - probably trained to use\n"
"it, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"她当时带着枪，很可能也受过\n"
"用枪训练。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/6
msgid ""
"Don't blame yourself. You couldn't have stopped\n"
"her anyway. You were unarmed.\n"
msgstr ""
"别自责。反正你也阻止不了\n"
"她。你当时手无寸铁。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/7
msgid ""
"I could at least have talked to her...\n"
msgstr ""
"至少我还能跟她说上话……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/8
msgid ""
"If I'd promised not to tell anyone, Paz wouldn't\n"
"have gone and done what she did...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果我答应不告诉任何人，Paz就不会\n"
"去做那些事了……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/9
msgid ""
"It's just... It's just... I was so shocked, I panicked -\n"
"ran away...\n"
msgstr ""
"只是……只是……我太震惊，慌了，\n"
"逃走了……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/10
msgid ""
"Chico... when you saw Paz, she was trying to\n"
"sabotage it, right?\n"
msgstr ""
"Chico……你看到Paz时，她正试图\n"
"破坏它，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/11
msgid ""
"Huh? Well, yeah...\n"
msgstr ""
"咦？嗯，是啊……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/12
msgid ""
"And right after that, she took control of it - tried\n"
"to make me surrender.\n"
msgstr ""
"紧接着，她控制住了它——试图\n"
"逼我投降。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/13
msgid ""
"Something doesn't add up.\n"
msgstr ""
"有点说不通。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/14
msgid ""
"Why would she sabotage ZEKE when she was\n"
"about to use it against me?\n"
msgstr ""
"她明明要用ZEKE来对付我，\n"
"为什么还要破坏它？\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/15
msgid ""
"Her actions were inconsistent, even for a spy.\n"
msgstr ""
"她行为矛盾，间谍也不该这样。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/16
msgid ""
"If she wanted to destroy ZEKE, she could have\n"
"done it and run away.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果她想毁掉ZEKE，她大可以\n"
"动手然后逃走。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/17
msgid ""
"But if her goal was to steal ZEKE, she'd have no\n"
"motive to sabotage it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但如果她的目标是偷走ZEKE，就没\n"
"动机去破坏它。\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/18
msgid ""
"I don't know...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道……\n"

#: codec/1/218/0xdaa90/19
msgid ""
"Maybe your seeing her caused her to change her\n"
"plan? I don't get it...\n"
msgstr ""
"也许你看到她让她改变了\n"
"计划？我搞不懂……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 376..1156
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/0
msgid ""
"...You think Paz was planning to double-cross\n"
"Cipher?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你觉得Paz打算背叛\n"
"Cipher？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 1170..2006
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/1
msgid ""
"Without ZEKE, she wouldn't have any way to\n"
"threaten you.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有ZEKE，她就没有任何办法\n"
"威胁你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 2020..3051
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/2
msgid ""
"If that were the case, she could have told me all\n"
"that from the beginning.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果是那样，她一开始就可以\n"
"把这一切都告诉我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 3092..3761
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/3
msgid ""
"She wouldn't have had to try and sabotage it.\n"
msgstr ""
"她根本不必去破坏它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 3775..4096
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/4
msgid ""
"I guess so...\n"
msgstr ""
"大概……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 4123..5851
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/5
msgid ""
"But that was the day before Peace Day. Paz was\n"
"going to sing in a band. I couldn't wait to hear her.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那是和平日的前一天。Paz要\n"
"在乐队里唱歌。我迫不及待想听她唱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 5907..7397
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/6
msgid ""
"What if she wasn't going to double cross them...\n"
"maybe she just wanted to at least be able to enjoy\n"
"that...\n"
msgstr ""
"如果她不是要背叛他们……\n"
"也许她只是想至少能享受\n"
"那件事……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 7425..7718
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/7
msgid ""
"Chico...\n"
msgstr ""
"奇科……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 7746..8818
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/8
msgid ""
"I knew it... If only I hadn't run away...\n"
msgstr ""
"我就知道……没逃就好了……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 8832..9835
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/9
msgid ""
"If I'd talked to her... promised I wouldn't tell\n"
"anybody...\n"
msgstr ""
"要是我跟她谈过……答应不告诉\n"
"别人……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 9849..11270
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/10
msgid ""
"Don't second-guess yourself. Think about who\n"
"might have been hurt if you'd kept quiet.\n"
msgstr ""
"别事后怀疑自己。想想如果你保持沉默，\n"
"可能会有人受到伤害。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 11298..11563
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/11
#: codec/1/253/0xfda60/13
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"可……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 11577..12524
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/12
msgid ""
"Besides, we don't know for sure she's dead.\n"
msgstr ""
"再说，我们也不确定她死了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 12552..13709
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/13
msgid ""
"She was ejected into the ocean. And she had\n"
"scuba equipment with her.\n"
msgstr ""
"她被弹射进海里。而且她带着\n"
"潜水装备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 13736..13973
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/14
#: codec/2/909/0x38db70/1
#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/1
msgid ""
"Yeah...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 13987..15450
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/15
msgid ""
"Stop beating yourself up over the past, Chico - put\n"
"your hope in the future.\n"
msgstr ""
"别再为过去自责了，奇科——把\n"
"希望寄托在未来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 15478..16676
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/16
msgid ""
"The past is the past, but the future is up to you.\n"
msgstr ""
"过去已过去，未来由你决定。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0130_010_0
#. timeline 16732..17136
#: codec/1/219/0xdb190/17
msgid ""
"...Right, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"……明白，BOSS。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 501..1365
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/0
msgid ""
"\"AI\" stands for artificial intelligence.\n"
msgstr ""
"“AI”是人工智能的缩写。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 1448..2479
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/1
msgid ""
"It refers to a manmade machine possessing an\n"
"intellect on par\n"
msgstr ""
"它指人造机器拥有\n"
"与人类同等的\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 2479..2883
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/2
msgid ""
"with that of a human being.\n"
msgstr ""
"智力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 2883..3287
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/3
msgid ""
"Is that even possible?\n"
msgstr ""
"这真有可能吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 3315..4151
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/4
msgid ""
"Possible? You've seen it with your own eyes.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能？你亲眼见过了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 4249..4973
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/5
msgid ""
"What the AI weapons are capable of.\n"
msgstr ""
"AI武器的能耐。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 4987..5935
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/6
msgid ""
"How Peace Walker carried out The Boss' will in the\n"
"end.\n"
msgstr ""
"和平行者最终如何\n"
"执行了THE BOSS的意志。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 5990..7105
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/7
msgid ""
"No mere machine could ever choose to sacrifice\n"
"itself like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有机器能那样\n"
"自我牺牲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 7161..8317
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/8
msgid ""
"I just can't see how a bunch of circuits and\n"
"switches could have a will of its own...\n"
msgstr ""
"我就是想不通一堆电路和\n"
"开关怎么会有自己的意志……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0010_000_1
#. timeline 8373..9780
#: codec/1/219/0xdb7c0/9
msgid ""
"It's called The Ghost in the Machine, Snake... And it\n"
"exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"这叫机器中的幽灵，SNAKE……它\n"
"确实存在。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/0
msgid ""
"Let's say, hypothetically, there really was an\n"
"intelligent machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"假设真的存在\n"
"有智能的机器。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/1
msgid ""
"How would you prove it?\n"
msgstr ""
"你要怎么证明？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/2
msgid ""
"What's the difference between a high-level\n"
"computer and an AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"高性能计算机和AI\n"
"有什么区别？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/3
msgid ""
"It depends on what you choose to define as\n"
"intelligence...\n"
msgstr ""
"这取决于你如何\n"
"定义「智能」……\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/4
msgid ""
"For example, Snake, listen to my voice talking to\n"
"you now. Suppose it were an AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"比如Snake，你现在听着我的声音。\n"
"假如我是AI呢？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/5
msgid ""
"Say what?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/6
msgid ""
"What if the living, breathing me, sitting here\n"
"drinking tea and talking to you,\n"
msgstr ""
"假如这个有血有肉、\n"
"坐着喝茶跟你说话的我，\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/7
msgid ""
"were actually an AI, programmed to simulate my\n"
"thoughts and my voice?\n"
msgstr ""
"其实是个AI，\n"
"被设定来模仿我的思想和声音？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/8
msgid ""
"You're nuts.\n"
msgstr ""
"你疯了。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/9
msgid ""
"No, I'm not. You couldn't prove I was a real human\n"
"being, could you?\n"
msgstr ""
"我没疯。你也证明不了\n"
"我是真正的人类，对吧？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/10
msgid ""
"It'd be... No.\n"
msgstr ""
"那……不会。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/11
msgid ""
"Hm. So if an AI is so advanced you can't tell it\n"
"from the real thing,\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯。那么如果AI先进到\n"
"你分不清真假，\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/12
msgid ""
"wouldn't you call that intelligence?\n"
msgstr ""
"那不就是智能吗？\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/13
msgid ""
"I'm not quite convinced.\n"
msgstr ""
"我还是不太信服。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/14
msgid ""
"But that's only one way to look at it.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过这也只是一种看法。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/15
msgid ""
"It's roughly how Dr. Turing explained artificial\n"
"intelligence.\n"
msgstr ""
"这大致就是图灵博士\n"
"对人工智能的解释。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/16
msgid ""
"The test I described is called the Turing Test in his\n"
"honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"我说的那个测试，\n"
"为纪念他而叫图灵测试。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/17
msgid ""
"Yeah, well, it sounds like a bad joke to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"哼，我听着像个拙劣的玩笑。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/18
msgid ""
"That singing monster of yours put me through hell.\n"
msgstr ""
"你那只唱歌的怪物可把我害惨了。\n"

#: codec/1/219/0xdbb50/19
msgid ""
"If I never meet one again, it'll be too soon.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好再也别让我碰上。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/0
msgid ""
"Dr. Alan Turing is known as the father of computer\n"
"science.\n"
msgstr ""
"艾伦·图灵博士被称为计算机\n"
"科学之父。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/1
msgid ""
"It was he who formulated the basic theory of AI.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是他创立了AI的基本理论。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/2
msgid ""
"During the war, he worked for GC&CS.\n"
msgstr ""
"战时他为GC&CS工作。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/3
msgid ""
"The government's cryptology school... the one that\n"
"broke Enigma.\n"
msgstr ""
"政府的密码学校……就是\n"
"破译恩尼格玛那所。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/4
msgid ""
"The very same.\n"
msgstr ""
"正是。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/5
msgid ""
"Without him, they might never have been able to\n"
"decipher the Germans' code.\n"
msgstr ""
"没有他，他们也许永远无法\n"
"破译德国人的密码。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/6
msgid ""
"...But then they arrested him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……后来他被捕了。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/7
msgid ""
"Why? Weren't his some of the greatest\n"
"contributions to winning the war?\n"
msgstr ""
"为什么？他不是为赢得战争\n"
"做出了巨大贡献吗？\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/8
msgid ""
"Homosexuality was a crime in Britain back then.\n"
"And he was gay.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时同性恋在英国是犯罪。\n"
"而他是同性恋。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/9
msgid ""
"I know exactly how crushed he was. I feel it's my\n"
"duty to further his AI research...\n"
msgstr ""
"我清楚他多崩溃。继续推进他的AI研究\n"
"是我的责任……\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/10
msgid ""
"Like \"The Imitation Game,\" huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"像《模仿游戏》？\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/11
msgid ""
"Ah, you know it, then?\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，你知道？\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/12
msgid ""
"The clue that inspired the Turing Test came from\n"
"a trifling little party game.\n"
msgstr ""
"启发图灵测试的线索来自\n"
"一个微不足道的派对小游戏。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/13
msgid ""
"You exchange written notes with another person\n"
"behind a screen,\n"
msgstr ""
"你与另一个人隔着屏幕\n"
"交换书面留言，\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/14
msgid ""
"and try to guess their gender whether they're a\n"
"woman,\n"
msgstr ""
"并猜他们性别，看是\n"
"女人，\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/15
msgid ""
"or a man pretending to be a woman....\n"
msgstr ""
"还是装成女人的男人……\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/16
msgid ""
"It's surprisingly difficult to tell the difference. Man\n"
"or woman, human or machine...\n"
msgstr ""
"要分辨出差异出奇地困难。男人\n"
"还是女人，人类还是机器……\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/17
msgid ""
"What do the differences even mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"区别意味着什么？\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/18
msgid ""
"Dr. Turing was fascinated by the differences\n"
"between men and women.\n"
msgstr ""
"图灵博士对男人与女人之间的差异\n"
"十分着迷。\n"

#: codec/1/220/0xdc290/19
msgid ""
"Perhaps that's what led him to formulate his test.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许正因如此他才提出了那个测试。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 487..1421
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/0
msgid ""
"What if you hadn't used The Boss as the model for\n"
"the AI?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你没把“Boss”当作\n"
"AI模型，会怎样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 1713..3078
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/2
msgid ""
"If the end goal is MAD, seems like there are more\n"
"suitable models out there.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果最终目标是MAD，看起来还有更\n"
"合适的模型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 3190..4569
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/3
msgid ""
"A military chief of staff, or a nuclear technician...\n"
"even the President.\n"
msgstr ""
"一位军队参谋长，或一名核技术员……\n"
"甚至总统。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 4709..5837
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/4
msgid ""
"Patriotism, leadership, good judgment...\n"
msgstr ""
"爱国心、领导力、判断力……\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 5962..7760
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/5
msgid ""
"Each of those qualities is essential when deciding\n"
"whether to launch a nuke, and she had them all.\n"
msgstr ""
"在决定是否发射核弹时，这些特质\n"
"每一项都至关重要，而她全都具备。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 8066..8470
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/6
msgid ""
"Wouldn't the President, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"总统不也是？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 8484..9557
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/7
msgid ""
"It's not enough. She had the will for it.\n"
msgstr ""
"不够。她有那份意志。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 9599..9835
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/8
msgid ""
"Will?\n"
msgstr ""
"意志？\n"

#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 9877..11270
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/9
msgid ""
"Let me explain, Snake. Peace Walker is a\n"
"stand-alone weapon.\n"
